      "Language": "pol",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The purpose of this study was to present the actual possibilities of bronchial asthma exacerbation control. The role of viral infection, especially, human metapneumovirus infection may be a leading cause of disease exacerbation in children population. Prevalence of gastroesophageal reflux had been detected in 24% of asthmatic patients, in some cases as a cause of asthma exacerbation. Glucocorticosteroid therapy is accepted as cardinal in asthma exacerbation, but some adverse effects create a control limit."},
